+wolfTrust STM32H5 Zephyr notes
+##############################
+
+This tree is carried by wolfTrust's in-repo patch series for the
+``tests/firmware/zephyr-stm32h5`` workflow.
+
+The intended non-secure target is ``nucleo_h563zi/ns`` with:
+
+* no TF-M handoff
+* the non-secure image linked into the wolfTrust guest flash slots
+* the non-secure RAM region carved to a single guest window
+* a devicetree node describing the wolfTrust TEE provider
+
+The first consumer is a pair of local NS guest applications:
+
+* guest0: active wolfTrust client
+* guest1: passive supervisor sidecar
+
+Further driver integration is carried by wolfTrust's Zephyr extra-module.
